<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="103" project="spaarke-ontology-platform-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Ontology admin slice (c): Classification admin</title>
    <phase>10 Ontology admin (D-22)</phase>
    <gate>104, 008, 057, 072 complete</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Admin writes to sprk_triagecategory, a cross-domain table that changes classifier behaviour on the next enrichment.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>List, form and three writes over one table, all as the caller.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>104, 008, 057, 072</deps>
    <tags>bff-api,frontend,admin,classifier,endpoints</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-6 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Build the Classification area of Ontology admin: triage categories with guidance, On/Off, which rules read each, 30-day volume, an edit form, rename blocked while a rule reads the category, and new categories saving Off, all written through the BFF as the caller.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE full-stack developer. A category edit is live on the next enrichment; treat it as production configuration.</role>
  <goal>An administrator can create, edit and enable triage categories from the Console, and cannot rename one a rule depends on.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>D-22 slice (c); reconciliation M-10: categories with guidance, On/Off, which rules read each, 30-day volume, recall vs the 80% / 50-item floor; edit in a form; rename blocked while a rule reads it; a new category saves Off. Task 008 grants Spaarke Ontology Administrator Create/Write/Read on sprk_triagecategory (D-22). Rules reference categories by GUID, so a rename does not break evaluation but does change the constrained-decoding enum name (NFR-09). #44: 30-day volume is available today from sprk_communication.sprk_triagecategory + sprk_receiveddate. Where measured recall is stored is reconciliation C-16, undecided.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Ontology/OntologyAdminClassificationEndpoints.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ontology/OntologyAdminClassificationService.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/OntologyAdmin/Classification</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.Ledger.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="owner">Scope (D-22): every write runs AS THE CALLER (IDataverseUserClient); no service-identity write to sprk_triagecategory.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: "which rules read each" is computed by scanning the enabled and draft policy versions' bodies for the category GUID; rename (sprk_name change) is refused while any version references it; a new category saves with enabled = No.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: recall is NOT built: where it is stored is undecided (C-16, spec section 11.1 O-10). Show recall only if task 074 or an owner decision has provided a source; otherwise omit the column.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: no confidence calibration (#5: no classifier confidence exists).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope (NFR-10, D-29): census entries; single 403 for an unresolved caller.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: if this task changes src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api, state the Placement Justification in the PR citing .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md, and measure publish size against a FRESH build of master from a short path with file counts compared on both sides. Ceiling 60 MB.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">Scope: tokens only; light and dark correct.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: before opening a BFF PR, run /conflict-check (sprk_triagecategory is shared with the email-communication domain).</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Classification administration</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/004-seed-policy-rows.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/v4-reconciliation.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/spec.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare the rigor level and reason per root CLAUDE.md section 8, then load the knowledge files above before touching code. Record the reconciliation section B.6 pre-start check (HANDOFF section 8 L303) in notes.</step>
    <step order="1">Implement the read (list with rule references and 30-day volume) and the create / update / enable routes as the caller.</step>
    <step order="2">Build the list and edit form with the task 057 kit.</step>
    <step order="3">Integration tests as the admin and as a Console User; a rename refused while a rule reads the category.</step>
    <step order="4">Update tasks/TASK-INDEX.md: set this task to the completed marker, AND set this POML status element to completed. Both, or scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1 fails the next push.</step>
    <step order="5">Record any deviation from this POML in projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>Recall storage (C-16) is undecided: before adding any recall column or reading 074's fixture for admin, STOP and ask the owner.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>sprk_triagecategory rows are authored in Dataverse directly (task 004); no admin route or UI exists; task 072 makes the guidance live in prompts.</existing>
    <extension>No existing admin surface to extend; the kit and tab shell are reused.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Criterion 8 (a new category with guidance changes classifier behaviour with no deployment) can only be exercised by editing rows outside the Console, and nothing stops a rename that silently changes a rule's decoding enum.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Rename blocked while referenced">
      <steps>
        <step>Open Fee / rate change and try to rename it</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>The rename is refused with the referencing rule named.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Dark mode compliance per ADR-021">
      <steps>
        <step>Toggle dark mode</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>All surfaces adapt.</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build and test .NET</tool>
    <tool name="npm">Build the client packages</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ontology/OntologyAdminClassificationService.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Ontology/OntologyAdminClassificationEndpoints.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/OntologyAdmin/Classification</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the admin, when the list loads, then each category shows guidance, On/Off, the rules that read it and its 30-day volume.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a new category, when saved, then it is created disabled; given an edit of guidance, then it is saved as the caller.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: renaming a category referenced by any policy version is refused, naming the rule.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a Console User is refused by every write route; an unresolved caller gets 403; every route is in the census.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no recall or calibration figure is shown unless a decided source exists.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Tests cover the stated contract and authorization cases; anything beyond needs a one-line justification in task notes. Both sides build.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>spec.md FR-59; D-22; reconciliation M-10, C-16; #41, #44.</notes>

  <execution><skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill></execution>
</task>
